1
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:23,870
This video demonstrates the donning and doffing of the following PPE.

2
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:30,770
Gown, gloves, disposable face mask, and face shield.

3
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:44,070
The first step is to remove personal items, such as jewelry, watches, coats, jackets, cell phones, pens, or additional bags,

4
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:48,570
and place them in a location outside of the laboratory.

5
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:53,570
Then, tie back any long hair if present.

6
00:00:53,570 --> 00:01:02,070
Next, gather your solid front wrap-around gown with tight-knit cuffs, a single pair of gloves,

7
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:10,570
a disposable face mask, or an N95 respirator, and a disposable face shield.

8
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:17,070
The decision whether to use a disposable face mask or an N95 respirator

9
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:24,070
will depend on the laboratory site-specific and activity-specific risk assessment.

10
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:32,070
Please note, this scenario will demonstrate donning and doffing a disposable face mask.

11
00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:36,070
Make sure you have the right size gown and gloves.

12
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:44,070
And don't forget to visually inspect all of your PPE for rips, tears, loose or missing straps,

13
00:01:44,070 --> 00:01:49,070
and replace any defective PPE you do find.

14
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:56,070
Next, pull on the gown, fastening it securely behind your neck and back or side.

15
00:01:56,070 --> 00:02:03,070
Do not tie it in a knot or fasten it so tightly that you cannot easily remove it later.

16
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:08,070
Make sure the gown fits well to allow for easy movement.

17
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:12,070
Street clothing should not be exposed.

18
00:02:12,070 --> 00:02:18,070
Next, put on your disposable face mask with ear loops behind your ears,

19
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:22,070
ensuring a snug fit against your face.

20
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:29,070
With your index finger of both hands, press down on each side of the flexible nose piece

21
00:02:29,070 --> 00:02:35,070
so that the top of the face mask fits snugly against your nose and cheeks.

22
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:41,070
Put on the disposable face shield and stretch to expand the elastic strap

23
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:47,070
and place it behind your head with the foam resting just above your eyebrows.

24
00:02:47,070 --> 00:02:52,070
Adjust the strap so that it fits snugly against your face.

25
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:57,070
Face shields must cover your forehead, extend below your chin,

26
00:02:57,070 --> 00:03:01,070
and wrap around the sides of your face.

27
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:05,070
And finally, put on your gloves.

28
00:03:05,070 --> 00:03:10,070
First, pull the gown's knit cuff down around the palm of your hand

29
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:15,070
and then pull the glove over, not under, the cuff.

30
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:18,070
This helps ensure your sleeves won't slip out

31
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:23,070
and the knit cuff won't be exposed to hazardous materials during work.

32
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:28,070
Ensure there are no punctures or tears in the gloves before beginning work.

33
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:34,070
The following steps describe one method and sequence of doffing PPE

34
00:03:34,070 --> 00:03:38,070
from most contaminated to least contaminated.

35
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:43,070
Other methods and sequences may vary based on the laboratory site-specific

36
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:46,070
and activity-specific risk assessments,

37
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:51,070
the procedures being conducted, and the PPE worn.

38
00:03:51,070 --> 00:03:56,070
The first step of doffing your PPE is removing your gown.

39
00:03:56,070 --> 00:04:02,070
To do this, untie the gown at your waist, grasp the gown's shoulders

40
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:06,070
and pull the gown forward, releasing the neck closure.

41
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:10,070
Pull the gown off of your shoulders and away from your body,

42
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:13,070
rolling the gown inside out as you go.

43
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:18,070
Once off your shoulders, remove your arms from the sleeves.

44
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:21,070
Before completely pulling off the gown sleeves,

45
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:26,070
pinch the gloves and sleeve together to help peel off the gloves.

46
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:30,070
Roll the gloves and gown inside out into a bundle.

47
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:35,070
Take care to prevent the potentially contaminated outside of the gown and gloves

48
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:39,070
from touching your bare hands and your street clothes.

49
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:43,070
Dispose of the bundle into the biohazard waste container.

50
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:49,070
Apply alcohol-based hand sanitizer with at least 60% ethanol

51
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:53,070
or 70% isopropanol to your hands.

52
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:58,070
Wash your hands with soap and water or don a new pair of gloves.

53
00:04:58,070 --> 00:05:02,070
Tilt your head slightly forward to take off your face shield.

54
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:07,070
Grasp the straps above the ears and gently lift the face shield

55
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:11,070
away from your face, taking care to avoid touching the shield itself,

56
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:14,070
which may be potentially contaminated.

57
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:20,070
Then discard the disposable face shield in the biohazard waste container.

58
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:24,070
To remove your disposable face mask, remove the ear loops,

59
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:28,070
taking care to avoid touching the potentially contaminated

60
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:31,070
exterior surface of the face mask.

61
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:34,070
Pull the face mask away from your face

62
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:38,070
and dispose of it in the biohazard waste container.

63
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:42,070
Last, wash your hands with soap and water.

64
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:49,070
Lather the backs of your hands, between your fingers, and under your nails.

65
00:05:49,070 --> 00:05:52,070
Scrub for at least 20 seconds.

66
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:57,070
Washing your hands with soap and water is the best method.

67
00:05:57,070 --> 00:06:00,070
However, if soap and water are unavailable,

68
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:05,070
an alcohol-based hand sanitizer containing at least 60% ethanol

69
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:11,070
or 70% isopropanol can be used as a temporary solution

70
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:15,070
until soap and water are available.

71
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:18,070
Additional considerations

72
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:21,070
Closed-toed shoes with solid and impermeable uppers

73
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:23,070
should be worn in the laboratory.

74
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:28,070
PPE will vary based on a laboratory site-specific

75
00:06:28,070 --> 00:06:31,070
and activity-specific risk assessment.

76
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:36,070
Donning and doffing areas should be physically separated from each other

77
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:40,070
to avoid contamination of cleaned PPE and personal belongings

78
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:44,070
with potentially contaminated PPE.

79
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:48,070
Donning and doffing procedures vary per institution.

80
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:52,070
Follow institutional policies and procedures.

81
00:06:52,070 --> 00:06:56,070
For additional training and workforce development resources,

82
00:06:56,070 --> 00:07:01,070
please visit cdc.gov slash labtraining

83
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:04,070
and click on the Job Aids button.
